; VU1 microprogram (generated by tools/vu1/gen.py fx, do not edit): effect particles (fx.c, FX_VU1 builds). One
; input vertex per particle; the program looks up its size / colour curves, rolls, projects and expands it into a
; 4-vertex triangle strip (the first two vertices of each particle carry ADC, so the strip restarts per particle).
; Constants: 0-3 view matrix columns, 4 scale (F, -F, Zs, fog a), 5 offset (cx, cy, 0, fog b) (vu1_begin +
; vu1_map_fog), 8-12 sin / cos coefficients (vu1_fx_begin). Batch (input buffer, BASE 16 / OFFSET 271):
; 0 {particles (even), -, -, -}, 1 (cw, ch, 0.5, 1 / fpr), 2 (0.5 / W - cw / 2, 0.5 / H, 0, fpr), 3 (du, dv, 0, edge
; fog a2), 4 (du, 0, 0, 0), 5 (0, dv, 0, 0), 6 (fog min, fog max, 0, 2048), 7 A+D GIF tag (6 regs: TEX0 TEX1 TEST ALPHA
; ZBUF FOGCOL, EOP) + 8-13, 14 PRIM tag template (EOP, triangle strip, STQ RGBAQ XYZF2), 15.. 8 curve
; tables of 8 keys x {size (kx, ky), colour (r, g, b, a)}, 143.. particles: {world xyz, 8 table + 7 age / life},
; {half size x, y, roll (-pi..pi), frame + 0.5}. cw / ch: flipbook cell, du / dv = cell - 1 texel (normalized).
; Per particle: view v = M p; key k, f from .w: size = mix(K_k, K_k+1, f) x half size, colour likewise; corner =
; centre + qx A + qy B with A = (hx cos, hy sin), B = (-hx sin, hy cos) (roll, then size, as fx.c's EE path);
; screen xy at q = 1 / v.z; depth and fog at z' = v.z - max(hx, hy) (pulled toward the camera, fx.c); fog =
; min(clamp(a z' + b, fmin, fmax), max(b + a2 z', 0)); cell (col, row) of frame n: row = trunc(n / fpr).
; sin / cos: half angle polynomials (x <= pi / 2), then the double angle (|error| < 2e-4).
; Output slots 558 / 751 (1 + 12 x 16 qw, alternating; VI08 keeps the next across batches).

; loop: 88 cycles per particle in the tools/vu1 timing model (2 per pass)
; layout: FX_IN 16 (271 qw each), FX_OUT0 558, FX_OUT1 751 (193 qw each), end 944

		.vu
		.align 4
		.global VU1Fx_CodeStart
		.global VU1Fx_CodeEnd
